# 3.1 Background on Video LLMs Inference

The inference process of video LLMs involves three key stages: before LLM, prefilling, and decoding.

(1) Before LLM. Given an input video with $B$ frames, a vision encoder processes each frame to produce $N _ { v }$ embedding vectors. These are projected into the text embedding space, yielding visual tokens $H _ { v } \in \mathbb R ^ { B N _ { v } 	imes d }$ , where $d$ represents the dimension of the hidden state space. A text prompt T = {ti}Nqi=1 is tokenized and embedded into text tokens $H _ { q } \in \mathbb { R } ^ { N _ { q } 	imes d }$ similarly. Finally, the visual and text tokens are concatenated to form $H = \mathrm { c o n c a t } [ H _ { v } , \dot { H } _ { q } ]$ , which serves as the LLM input.

