(3) Decoding Stage. The decoding stage generates tokens autoregressively, leveraging the KV cache. At each time step $t$ , only the new token $h _ { t }$ is processed to compute its key and value representations, avoiding recalculating attention weights over the entire history. The KV cache is updated by appending the new key-value pairs: $\mathbf { K } \gets [ \mathbf { K } , h _ { t } \mathbf { W } _ { K } ] , \mathbf { V } \gets [ \mathbf { V } , h _ { t } \mathbf { W } _ { V } ]$ . This caching mechanism substantially reduces the computational complexity of the generation process.

